    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 57,
        "text": "Hi, Daniel. You look busy. What are you working on?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "d6131d3c232e35153d4c36b68e49b68f1b7edbe4645bf520af894cd78fc6785f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 66,
        "sourceEnd": 190,
        "text": "I'm helping the Riverside Community Archive. We collect old photos and letters from local families. Then we put them online.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "1f5f9b6e75761faf5498e849cc991fca80008e88ac3e6337b484e8d077ddf16c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 197,
        "sourceEnd": 298,
        "text": "That sounds nice. But I have a question. Do you ask people before you put their family photos online?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "5f7bb307040cafdefe214b3598ff737257dbd725da0d524b06a4d0e73a38e476",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 307,
        "sourceEnd": 481,
        "text": "Yes, we do. We always ask for written permission. Last month, a woman named Mrs. Chen gave us a box of letters. She signed a form, and she chose which letters we could share.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "f538c7af7d9bba753a5524906d42021b26d48fceb6886d64931b632f9c2e6a5b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 488,
        "sourceEnd": 555,
        "text": "Good. But what about people in the photos? Maybe they didn't agree.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "7475ae94eb7690df3a81205fef0b7d5fd7ec28e384d3c669a906d3c161175909",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 564,
        "sourceEnd": 813,
        "text": "That's a real problem. We learned that lesson last year. We uploaded a photo of a school class from 1965. One man in the photo called us. He was angry because he didn't want his childhood picture on the internet. We took the photo down the same day.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "05b2b949d7659f016d91a1c10d4021b3d34009a91fc8dd4ccb832ef767dc91e8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 820,
        "sourceEnd": 845,
        "text": "So what is your rule now?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "5f6c92aca3433b8fc1a03cabb542bacf4d30ed0cde715f9d400974cd1547e56e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 854,
        "sourceEnd": 1086,
        "text": "Now we have three rules. First, we ask the person who owns the item. Second, if the photo shows living people, we try to contact them. Third, if someone says no, we don't share it. We keep it in the archive building, but not online.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "ae888116356aac9559d59df4a5cc86b57e9fac027a9feb84e320ef167c1e5327",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1093,
        "sourceEnd": 1147,
        "text": "That sounds fair. But contacting everyone sounds hard.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "44192de467671f951c31e4bf3a03f9ff9cfe5148518300cdcb8b25ee98299a4c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1156,
        "sourceEnd": 1343,
        "text": "It is hard. Sometimes we can't find people. Then we don't publish the photo. We only publish photos of people who have agreed, or photos where everyone in the picture is no longer living.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "602dfba82cfe3c1fa9eb24e0af403103c5f05d43ad1513031dc41986d2758637",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1350,
        "sourceEnd": 1411,
        "text": "Wait, is that last rule okay? Some families might still care.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "d83776c7df95c739ca3f5ee8bcaf5103566ab5f8f830d38cc4aa0aeeb8a3003d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1420,
        "sourceEnd": 1562,
        "text": "You're right. We changed that rule too. Now, even for old photos, we ask the family if we can find them. If we can't find the family, we wait.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "dee87597f67219b24774bbbe2ebd58a36daa905d0d291fa95a17e40f110310ee",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1569,
        "sourceEnd": 1646,
        "text": "I see. What about information like addresses or phone numbers in old letters?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "3a16c9f28a49598551258a40e82f86d678ee260f44f232026da26ee6ce2d308a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1655,
        "sourceEnd": 1904,
        "text": "We remove private details. For example, last week I read a letter from 1972. It had a home address and a phone number. I blacked them out before we put the letter online. The letter is still useful for history, but the private information is hidden.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a404accbffe9b6f6a4d01ce384bc861fa68636d66e035008e5058d437be28361",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1911,
        "sourceEnd": 1984,
        "text": "That's a good example. Do you also collect information from social media?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "6265124266310edd69aeec1fc5f732a99c4099b6d8f18c9dbc97dfa957de8718",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1993,
        "sourceEnd": 2162,
        "text": "No, we don't. We only use things that people give us directly. We don't copy posts from Facebook or WeChat. That would be wrong because people didn't give us permission.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "2538c355b9a7c400617779f3d144445aae3c01c293432c4eedfd4dc9cb7e23a9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2169,
        "sourceEnd": 2242,
        "text": "What if a person gives you information, but later they change their mind?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "3f653ed1ded43b261b34da37844f58126e055bb26cbc91ce89daafa102305e7a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2251,
        "sourceEnd": 2436,
        "text": "Then we remove it. Last spring, a man named Mr. Patel shared a recording of his father's stories. Two months later, he asked us to delete it. We deleted it immediately. We didn't argue.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "e5515f29c5fc1dd20130ec0468f19cb00db63bcbfb920cd5822fed2790e53c98",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2443,
        "sourceEnd": 2506,
        "text": "That's respectful. How do you explain your rules to the public?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "9c7a12f9666fa72511a806e4308c70fa718e82da0900ba480d0a7118d02bcf5b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2515,
        "sourceEnd": 2730,
        "text": "We have a short page on our website. It says: 'We ask first. We protect private details. We remove things when people ask.' We also give talks at the library. Next month, I'm giving a talk about why consent matters.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "3ace9b7c4bc4a95ebcee5f2bfdd2185e02ca76eae8721540648ec6c720083774",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2737,
        "sourceEnd": 2779,
        "text": "I'd like to come. Can I bring my students?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "3920a77bd3a957e4d100d09eae6eeb61b19dcfe4a5f02fa006379be26d87a9e0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2788,
        "sourceEnd": 2919,
        "text": "Of course. The talk is on Saturday at 2 p.m. It's free. But please tell me how many students are coming, because the room is small.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "39ea7b8bbded1059eab624f356722a5b78373079489af2224d3bc5820e917e69",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2926,
        "sourceEnd": 3002,
        "text": "I will. Thanks, Daniel. This conversation made me think about my own photos.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "357ad0816444b5a9f99a0f15e22c48df05447fadf101cb9eea95e83cc6e8042f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 3011,
        "sourceEnd": 3171,
        "text": "Me too. Actually, after our talk last year, I deleted some old photos of my friends from my phone. I didn't ask them before I posted those pictures. I felt bad.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a0236849b15905d6ee9da3ec5961d259377ae7dfcd8d9524dc8102d5f6a05a41",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3178,
        "sourceEnd": 3235,
        "text": "That's honest. So the rules are not just for the archive.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "1319ff18b7dbfbf2ef590061f623425b41648796625d44351290a5220a8be446",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 3244,
        "sourceEnd": 3309,
        "text": "Right. They are for everyone who collects and shares information.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "e4681dbdbd0350fe362151d9c5b1183dd3cecaaf6ad3b866a79b09f6948e54d3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
